          dealing: 'Dealer gives 3 cards to each player, then 2. The next card is turned face up. Players then bid to take the contract (Hokom/Sun or Pass). Once a contract is chosen, the dealer finishes the deal so everyone has 8 cards.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "The first team to reach 152 points wins. Points are earned from card values in tricks, the final trick bonus, and declared 'Projects'.",
          gameplay: 'Players must follow suit. If unable to follow in Hokom, you must play a trump card. The winner of the trick leads the next.',
          keyRules: [
            "Last Trick: The final trick provides an extra 10 points (called 'Abna'a').",
            'Card Points: Total card points in Sun = 130; in Hokom = 162.',
            "The 'Gawa': A specialized verbal challenge to double the score.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "In Hokom, lead your trumps early to exhaust the opponents' ability to ruff your winning Kings and Aces. In Sun, focus on establishing control through long suits.",
          intermediate: 'Watch the discards. If your partner discards a 7 of Spades, they are likely signals that they have no more Spades. Use this to lead Spades and let them trump in.',
          advanced: "The 'Lock' (Qafel): If you have the best trumps, you can 'lock' the game, meaning trumps cannot be led. This allows you to walk through with your long suit and wipe out the contractor.",
          tips: [
            "Always declare your projects early. A missed '100' declaration can cost you the entire game.",
            "If you are the contractor and have only 1 trump, don't bid Hokom; the Khosara penalty is too high.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
