          deckDescription: 'One standard 32-card deck: eight ranks (seven through ace) in each of four suits. No jokers; used for Baloot (Belote-style game popular in the Middle East) with trump and marriage scoring.',
          suitDescription: 'Four suits (typically French: spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Trump is determined by bidding or the turned card; follow suit when able. Marriage (king and queen of trump) scores bonus points.',
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit: seven, eight, nine, ten, jack, queen, king, ace. In trump the order differs (jack and nine are often high). Standard 32-card trick order applies for Baloot.',
